Drop the type-model fetch's progress line on stdout (Tuna Mail)

TypeModelProvider::fetch_server_model prints "Attempting to get base model
version?" to stdout whenever the server's type model hash changes. A library
has no business on its caller's stdout: it corrupts the reply line of a
stdio helper, and in process it lands in whatever the host process uses fd 1
for (a JVM's System.out under the Kotlin bindings). The line carries nothing
the SDK's own log calls do not, so it is removed rather than redirected.

